# A YubiKey's keyboard, the interface its OTP types through, refused as it
# arrives. Touched when nothing has asked for it, the key types a one-time
# password and presses Enter, and at the disk prompt that is a wrong PIN
# spent against the TPM's few tries. Its FIDO2 interface is HID too, but
# not a keyboard (protocol 0), and the smart card is CCID, so both keep
# working. The kernel unbinds the keyboard the moment it's refused.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_interface", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1050", \
  ATTR{bInterfaceClass}=="03", ATTR{bInterfaceProtocol}=="01", ATTR{authorized}="0"
